e><surname>Etter</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Perneger</surname><given-names>TV</given-names></name><name><surname>Ronchi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distributions of smokers by stage: international comparison and association with smoking prevalence</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>580</fpage><lpage>585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9245682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/pmed.1997.0179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Etter</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Associations between smoking prevalence, stages of change, cigarette consumption, and quit attempts across the United States</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>373</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14766121</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ypmed.2003.11.006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hardening and the hard-core smoker: concepts, evidence, and implications</article-title><source>Nicotine Tob Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12745505</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/1462220021000060428</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emery</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilpin</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ake</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Farkas</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierce</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterizing and identifying "hard-core" smokers: implications for further reducing smoking prevalence</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>387</fpage><lpage>394</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10705856</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WHO regional office for Europe</collab></person-group><article-title>European health for all database (HFA-DB) - Updated: June 2007</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.dk/document/tob/tobconf2002/edoc8.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Institute of Epidemiology and Social Medicine</collab></person-group><article-title>EU-Project - Measuring Tobacco Control from the General Population Perspective - European Survey On Tobacco Control Attitudes And Knowledge Introduction &#x02013; ESTA</article-title><year>2006</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.medizin.uni-greifswald.de/epidem/engl/eu/esta/index.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heatherton</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kozlowski</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>Frecker</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Fagerstrom</surname><given-names>KO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Fagerstrom Test for Nicotine Dependence: a revision of the Fagerstrom Tolerance Questionnaire</article-title><source>Br J Addict</source><year>1991</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>1119</fpage><lpage>1127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1932883</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1360-0443.1991.tb01879.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>John</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Schumann</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hapke</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Rumpf</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Adam</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Alte</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ludemann</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A short form of the Fagerstrom Test for Nicotine Dependence and the Heaviness of Smoking Index in two adult population samples</article-title><source>Addict Behav</source><year>2004</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>1207</fpage><lpage>1212</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15236824</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.addbeh.2004.03.019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prochaska</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>DiClemente</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stages of change in the modification of problem behaviors</article-title><source>Prog Behav Modif</source><year>1992</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1620663</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dijkstra</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>De Vries</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Subtypes of precontemplating smokers defined by different long-term plans to change their smoking behavior</article-title><source>Health Educ Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>434</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11066460</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/her/15.4.423</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laforge</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Velicer</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Richmond</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Owen</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stage distributions for five health behaviors in the United States and Australia</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9973589</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/pmed.1998.0384</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Velicer</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Fava</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Prochaska</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Abrams</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmons</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierce</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of smokers by stage in three representative samples</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>411</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7479632</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/pmed.1995.1065</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wewers</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Stillman</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartman</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Shopland</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of daily smokers by stage of change: Current Population Survey results</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>710</fpage><lpage>720</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12744915</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0091-7435(03)00044-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>West</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Time for a change: putting the Transtheoretical (Stages of Change) Model to rest</article-title><source>Addiction</source><year>2005</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>1036</fpage><lpage>1039</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16042624</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1360-0443.2005.01139.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Machin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bryant</surname><given-names>TN</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Statistics with Confidence - 2nd edition</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>London, BMJ Books</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>